# Clear, warn, note, and pause live here. ClearScreen is not called: a non-interactive host rejects it.
# AskName is the prompt sentence. Running does not wait for a person.
# Running returns 5.

To ClearScreen, returning nothing
    clear the screen

To AskName, returning a string
    the name is ask the user for "Your name"
    return the name

To Fail, returning an integer
    stop with "failed"
    return 0

When run, returning an integer
    note "host sample"
    warn "host sample"
    delay 1 ms
    say "host"
    the saved is the current folder
    the folder is the temp folder
    go to the folder
    go to the saved
    the score is 0
    if the length of the home folder is greater than 0
        increase the score
    if the length of the temp folder is greater than 0
        increase the score
    if the length of the current folder is greater than 0
        increase the score
    if the length of the script folder is greater than 0
        increase the score
    the user is the environment variable USERNAME
    if the length of the user is greater than 0
        increase the score
    return the score
